# Tablet Visual Regression Baselines — Placeholder

This folder is intentionally empty in the initial AAP delivery.

# Purpose

This folder stores tablet-viewport (768×1024) visual regression baseline PNGs
used by the Playwright `*-tablet` projects (`chromium-tablet`, `firefox-tablet`,
`webkit-tablet`) when running the eight visual specs in `tests/visual/*.spec.ts`.

# Why is this folder empty?

Per AAP Section 0.4.5 and Section 0.10.5, the Figma file
`2qR7NSTmQLynkmlj9B4ltc` provides only desktop-resolution (2880×2048 and
1104×854) renderings of the SSO frames. Tablet renderings at 768×1024
cannot be derived from these without distortion, so tablet baselines must
be captured from the freshly-implemented SSO components during the first
Playwright `--update-snapshots` run.

# Future Population Workflow

Once the SSO components are authored in a subsequent implementation cycle:

  1. Run:
       npx playwright test --update-snapshots tests/visual/ --project=chromium-tablet
     (and similarly for firefox-tablet, webkit-tablet)
  2. Playwright captures live screenshots of the SSO routes at 768×1024 viewport
     and writes them to this folder.
  3. A designer reviews each captured PNG against the Figma design intent
     (extrapolating from the desktop renderings).
  4. After designer sign-off, the eight tablet baselines are committed:
       - signin-a-microsoft-only.png
       - signin-b-microsoft-google.png
       - signin-c-see-more.png
       - signin-c-expanded.png
       - registration-completion.png
       - signup-error.png
       - link-accounts-microsoft.png
       - link-accounts-generic.png
  5. Future visual spec runs at the tablet projects will then diff
     against these committed baselines.
  6. Once at least one PNG is committed, this .gitkeep file MAY be removed.

